.TH GXWI-FILE-DIALOG 1 "2026-10-03" "Peios"
.SH NAME
gxwi-file-dialog \- choose a file to open, or a place to save one, in a dialog on a GXWI desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-file-dialog
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opened by another program, which wants a file chosen: one to read, or a
place and a name to write to. That program starts it as a child, on the
desktop it is on, and the two speak over the dialog's standard input and
output, one JSON object a line. The program's first line says whether a file
is to be opened or saved, what the dialog is called, what the file is for,
the folder to start in, the name to suggest, and the kinds of file to offer.
The dialog answers once, with the path chosen or that the person cancelled,
and ends. It never opens the file: the program does.
.PP
The dialog shows one folder at a time, its folders first, then its files of
the kind chosen. Opening a folder goes into it; Up goes to the folder above,
Home to the person's home folder, and a path typed anywhere. Hidden files
shows names that start with a dot. To open, the person picks a file; to save,
they type a name, which takes the extension of the kind chosen if it has
none, and saving over a file that is there asks first.
.PP
It is a small file manager as well: New folder makes a folder, and Rename and
Delete act on what is picked, a folder with everything in it, after asking.
The dialog runs as the person, and does all this as them. What they may not
do, it asks the system first, and offers it disabled, saying why; a folder
they may not list says so.
.PP
The dialog ends when it has answered, when it is closed or cancelled (Esc),
and when its standard input closes: when the program that opened it goes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/apps/dev.peios.gxwi-file-dialog.toml
Its application declaration, not listed in a launcher.
.SH SEE ALSO
PSPU \(sc9, File Choosing, at learn.peios.org, which sets out the protocol.
